+# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's zones
+
+## Symptom
+
+Every planned HR corridor showed up on the Forerunner as one of the watch's own
+zone bands (118–137, 151–162, 137–151, …) instead of the planned ranges
+(117–129, 151–160, 129–141, …), regardless of the watch's LTHR setting. The
+two earlier attempts failed differently: `units: "bpm"` rendered impossible
+values (214–249 bpm), and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` rendered a constant 101.
+
+## Root cause
+
+The generator sent each HR corridor as `{"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}`.
+In Intervals.icu's `workout_doc`, the lower bound of a range must be the key
+`start`, not `value`. The key name selects the FIT-export mode at Garmin sync:
+
+- `{value, end}` → exported as a lap-HR / zone-mapped target. The watch clamps
+  it to its own (auto-detected) zone bands — exactly the reported symptom.
+- `{start, end}` → exported as an instant-HR corridor: Intervals converts the
+  percentages to bpm using the threshold stored in Intervals (LTHR 172) and the
+  watch displays that raw corridor. Verified behavior from a published
+  reproduction of this exact issue: a 75–82% target rendered 129–141 bpm on the
+  watch even with watch LTHR 168 vs Intervals LTHR 172.
+
+This also explains the earlier failures: absolute `bpm` values were misread as
+percentages by the FIT export (hence 214–249), and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` are
+not schema keys at all, so the target was dropped and the watch fell back to
+its "no valid HR target" constant 101.
+
+## What I changed
+
+`gen.py`, `hr_target()` — one key rename:
+
+```python
+# before
+return {"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}
+# after
+return {"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}
+```
+
+Percentages of LTHR are kept (not precomputed bpm) deliberately: Intervals does
+the %→bpm conversion at export time from its own stored threshold, so the
+corridor stays correct even when the watch's auto-detected LTHR drifts.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` now emits `{"units": "%lthr", "start": …, "end": …}`
+  for all four distinct corridors (warm-up 68–75, tempo 88–93, float 75–82,
+  cool-down 65–72).
+- Expected watch display after the next push/sync, per Intervals LTHR 172:
+  117–129, 151–160, 129–141, 112–124 — the "expected" column in
+  `readback/watch-notes.md`.
+- Not re-pushed (no external calls per task constraints), so watch-side
+  confirmation is pending the next normal `push.sh` run.
+
+## Related trap (not changed)
+
+The Intervals web UI renders steps from a separate top-level `description`
+field in its text grammar (not from `workout_doc`), and an unparseable
+description can wipe both representations. Out of scope for this fix, but worth
+knowing if steps ever look wrong in the UI.
+
+Diagnosis confirmed against: "Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu
+API workouts — start/end, not value/end",
+https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts
